      "q": "How much does Department of Energy spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy spends $46B on contracts in FY2026 to date, across 3,881 awards with an average award size of $11.9M, and obligations fell 5.2% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Energy buy?",
      "a": "Energy buys a mix dominated by Facilities Support Services at $23.2B, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $6.9B and another R&D category at $3.4B. Other top purchases include Remediation Services at $2.9B, Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing at $2.8B, and various professional, technical, hazardous waste, and biotechnology R&D services."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Energy's largest contractors?",
